The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (unlikely(copied < len && !PageUptodate(page))) {
    copied = 0;
    goto out;
}
```
Reason:
This condition incorrectly prevents the page from being marked as up-to-date when the correct amount of data is written. If the number of bytes copied is less than the length and the page is not up-to-date, it sets `copied` to 0 and exits the function, leaving the page in a not up-to-date state even when the entire page size was written.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!PageUptodate(page)) {
    if (unlikely(copied < len)) {
        copied = 0;
        goto out;
    } else if (len == PAGE_SIZE) {
        SetPageUptodate(page);
    }
}
```
Reason:
The fix modifies the logic to check if the page is not up-to-date. If the entire page size is written (`len == PAGE_SIZE`), it explicitly sets the page as up-to-date using `SetPageUptodate(page)`, ensuring that the page reflects the correct state after a successful write operation.

